    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-statusline\n\n### Description\n\nApologies as I don't know how to properly add a title to this but what I'm asking is that\r\n\r\nI wanted to have 2 sections where the first section contains the base dir and the last contains the filename (tail). What I want to do is to apply a bold style only to the second section.\r\n\r\nI've somewhat achieved it but there's a gap between the first and second section\r\n<img width=\"1038\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/10972027/6c25a463-120f-47d2-bd85-f25ddcf6a997\">\r\n\r\nIs it possible to remove it?\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-23T16:06:37Z",
